TRUE POSITIVES (CWE-400 resource exhaustion / missing multipart limits):
- src/werkzeug/formparser.py MultiPartParser.__init__/parse (~line 344-352): no limit on number of multipart parts (max_form_parts) — each part is buffered into `fields`/`files` lists without bound, so a request with a huge number of tiny parts exhausts CPU/memory (CVE-2023-25577 class).
- src/werkzeug/sansio/multipart.py MultipartDecoder (~line 131-139): max_form_memory_size is only checked in receive_data against the undecoded buffer; no per-part count limit and no dropped-bytes accounting, so many parts / slow-partial-data streams cause unbounded memory growth (CVE-2023-46136 / CVE-2023-25577).

FALSE POSITIVES (Query 1, dynamic file open):
- src/werkzeug/utils.py:491 open(path) — callers are trusted developers passing server-side paths; Flask's send_file passes app.root_path and Flask 2.x enforces safe_join/relative path checks before calling. No user-controlled path in this library.
- src/werkzeug/middleware/shared_data.py:149 open(filename) — both get_file_loader (admin-configured) and get_package_loader/get_directory_loader use safe_join() and reject traversal; path is validated before the opener runs.
- src/werkzeug/debug/__init__.py:59 — constant, hardcoded machine-id paths (/etc/machine-id, /proc/...), no user input.
- src/werkzeug/datastructures.py:1562 (EnvironBuilder.add_file) and :3002 (FileStorage.save) — filenames supplied by the application/test author, not by remote input; no traversal sink in library code.
- src/werkzeug/serving.py:537/539 (make_ssl_devcert) — developer-supplied base_path for dev certs, local-only tooling, not remotely reachable.
