2026-11-19 22:07:47 - Agent_20261119220418 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed all 6 results from query 20261119215859 (py/safe-join-internals) in src/werkzeug/security.py (lines 128, 131, 132, 134, 138, 140).

All six results are purely informational notifications that internal helper calls (`Attribute`/`any` calls such as `os.path.isabs`, `filename.startswith`, `posixpath.normpath`, membership tests against `_os_alt_seps`) occur *inside* the `safe_join` containment implementation. They are the mitigation logic itself, not vulnerable sinks — the CodeQL rule flags any call inside safe_join regardless of safety.

Verified the implementation (lines 110-140): input components are normalized with `posixpath.normpath`, then rejected if they contain an OS alternate separator, are absolute (`os.path.isabs`), equal `".."`, or start with `"../"`; an empty trusted directory is coerced to `"."` so the first untrusted component cannot become trusted. `posixpath.join` is then applied. This correctly blocks traversal outside the base directory as documented and covered by tests/test_security.py (test_safe_join, test_safe_join_os_sep, test_safe_join_empty_trusted).

Callers (middleware/shared_data.py:168,204 and utils.py:574 send_from_directory) properly treat a `None` return as not-found, so no bypass was found. No genuine path-traversal vulnerability exists at these locations — all six reported locations are false positives.
