2026-11-19 22:09:52 - Agent_20261119220418 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the single CodeQL result for Werkzeug 2.2.2's debugger (CVE-2024-34069, py/debug-host-identifiers at src/werkzeug/debug/__init__.py:439). Investigation of the DebuggedApplication `__call__` dispatcher, `pin_auth`, `check_pin_trust`, and `get_resource` confirmed that the debugger console/pin-auth endpoints do not validate the Host header, so DNS rebinding or a browser reaching the app through a non-local host allows an attacker to authenticate with a pin, obtain the secret via the printpin/resource endpoints, and then reach `execute_command` (arbitrary Python evaluation) resulting in RCE. No trusted_hosts enforcement exists anywhere in the debug middleware path. Submitted one true-positive finding for the missing Host/Origin validation on the interactive debugger, which enables CWE-306/CWE-94 (Werkzeug debugger RCE via DNS rebinding). The version file and test files were examined and excluded as non-exploitable.
